# #1748: a covariant type parameter inside an INVARIANT generic is refused by name. `list[T]` admits
# neither direction (Sharpy.List<T> is an invariant class), so this declaration was CS1961 behind
# SPY0908 — the C# compiler doing the refusing — and is now SPY0418 at the annotation.
interface ICovariant[out T]:
    def get_list(self) -> list[T]


def main():
    print("unreachable")
